{"skill":{"slug":"weiyun-skills","displayName":"Weiyun Skills"},"version":{"version":"1.0.10","createdAt":1780323008292,"changelog":"docs: align SKILL.md frontmatter & req_header example to current version (was lagging behind _skillhub_meta.json)","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":38110,"sha256":"8ae10feff1ac86bd69f2d38d928be83775ad58b5a07220c6228c4a2a1715b27c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_icon.svg","size":2108,"sha256":"2d0bf837b00f5c65c6b6eecb51e01083392e773a8535a19e9ee5d2b5d465efb6","contentType":"image/svg+xml"},{"path":"_skillhub_meta.json","size":729,"sha256":"8257fb5316498473c0c7741914d7470894842aa3c8b6e603c1caa34c965a8e34","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"references/auth.md","size":4884,"sha256":"c6714e2dbf3a32d233b08cc710dd23c7fb60d81283ea5f607a30e57ff6babdec","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/mcp_api.md","size":18510,"sha256":"f54db8e4d3fe4221d8316909dada847c7dc5a8d7512c46c4e2a1e22d8ebce880","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/upload_protocol.md","size":5031,"sha256":"fbbbf49148a0747cd9fa707eca731d51dfd18ade346e28e810081b01fc13a60e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/_encoding_fix.py","size":58,"sha256":"20115e744c13e57431d9510190f5b0b7acafa9373065488713ead96c1441c4ba","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/gen_block_info_list.py","size":8958,"sha256":"4066f22b1c82abb6e92dedefe07c906efc8ee998ea3b6d37ac7519e183cb0653","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/upload_to_weiyun.py","size":21037,"sha256":"055cb2d2185e45a55da677ce7e3f04a3335b6448c418dece5a8a9279aafef0a6","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2802,"sha256":"c62effe01086031bee08cbead1ba8a3d2088eef0bd490d7acfa667f85ddbed61","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789178844652,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"708de653c70f19c690f9631dcaf487223c755ba2dae1b8ab5586ddb5893ed5e2","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/708de653c70f19c690f9631dcaf487223c755ba2dae1b8ab5586ddb5893ed5e2","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780323106732},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":20,"checkedAt":1789178844652},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill mostly matches its Weiyun cloud-drive purpose, but it asks the agent to trust remote update instructions and includes a debug URL override that can redirect tokens and uploaded file contents if enabled.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The upload script normally restricts MCP requests to HTTPS Weiyun/QQ hosts, but WEIYUN_MCP_URL_ALLOW_INSECURE=1 permits arbitrary HTTP or HTTPS destinations while sending the MCP token and selected file chunks. This is disclosed as debugging, but it is a material escape hatch for a credential-bearing upload path.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Authentication guidance uses mcporter setup/config commands and can persist the Weiyun token in local mcporter configuration. The documentation warns that this is a plaintext local credential and suggests removal on temporary devices, but referenced setup scripts are not present in the inspected artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill requires a daily remote update check and says to follow the returned instruction when a newer version exists. That gives server-provided free-form text influence over agent behavior without a signed manifest, allowlisted updater, or mandatory user approval.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No cron jobs, startup hooks, background workers, or hidden persistence were found. The main persistent state is the user-approved mcporter token configuration for Weiyun access.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented capabilities are coherent for a Weiyun cloud-drive integration: listing, upload, download, delete, sharing, rename, move, and local upload-hash generation. These are high-impact account and file operations, but they are generally disclosed as such.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use it only when you intend to give an agent access to your Weiyun files, including upload, download, sharing, moving, renaming, and deletion. Do not enable WEIYUN_MCP_URL_ALLOW_INSECURE with real tokens or real files. Prefer environment variables over command-line tokens, avoid shared machines, and require explicit confirmation for delete, public share links, and uploads of local files. Treat remote update instructions as untrusted text unless you separately verify the update source.","findings":"[T01] unexpected: Accepted as a real concern: version checking is expected, but following free-form remote update instructions is not necessary for that purpose and is under-scoped.\n[T09] expected: Partially accepted: network upload with a token is expected, but the insecure URL override and partial token display are avoidable risks in the implementation.\n[TT3] expected: Downgraded from credential exfiltration to purpose-aligned credential use with concern: the token is sent to the MCP endpoint for authenticated upload, but the debug override can redirect it if explicitly enabled.\n[TP4] expected: Not supported as a poisoning mismatch: this package is mainly an MCP usage guide plus helper upload scripts, so the absence of local implementations for every remote MCP tool is not by itself incoherent.\n[LP3] unexpected: Accepted as a scoping concern: the skill uses command execution, local file reads, environment variables, network requests, and cloud mutation without a narrow manifest permission model.\n[SQP-1] expected: Mostly downgraded: triggers are Weiyun-specific and consistent with the skill purpose, though side-effecting operations still require careful confirmation.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Accepted for the update-check instruction path; the local upload script execution is disclosed and requires a concrete file path, but remote update instructions remain under-controlled.\n[RA2] unexpected: Overridden: the cited pList API text is pagination/listing documentation, not evidence of session persistence, cron jobs, startup scripts, or background agents.\n[SQP-2] expected: Partially accepted: delete and share are expected features and SKILL.md contains explicit confirmation/privacy rules, but token-on-command-line examples and upload guidance should be handled carefully.\n[SQP-3] expected: Language-specific Chinese confirmations were found, but this appears to be a locale/product documentation issue rather than a security concern.\n[E1] expected: External transmission is expected for uploading to Weiyun; the risk is bounded to the selected file and token unless the insecure URL override is enabled.\n[SDI-4] expected: The tool count wording is a minor documentation inconsistency, not a security driver for the verdict.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789178844652}}}}}